# Using azldev

azldev builds a Linux distribution from TOML configuration. It imports RPM specs
from an upstream distro and customizes them with an overlay system — no spec
forking. Components render to specs and sidecar build inputs, then build into RPMs;
images assemble RPMs into bootable artifacts.

## Orient yourself

- Run azldev from the repo root (where `azldev.toml` lives), or pass `-C <dir>`.
- Global, agent-friendly flags: **`-q`** (quiet) and **`-O json`** (machine-readable
  output). They work on every command.
- Config is a stitched TOML hierarchy: `azldev.toml` includes the distro and project
  config, which include the component files (`**/*.comp.toml`) into one namespace.

## Core concepts

- **Component** — a unit of packaging that renders to a spec and sidecar build inputs,
  then builds into one or more RPMs. Its spec source is upstream (default), a pinned
  upstream distro/version, or a local spec.
- **Overlay** — a semantic patch applied to a spec or source file at render time, so
  you customize upstream without forking it.
- **Distro** — a named build target (`*.distro.toml`) with upstream URIs, release
  versions, and build inputs.
- **Rendered spec** — the generated `.spec` after overlays; a build input, never
  hand-edited.
- **Upstream commit config** — generated component TOML pinning the resolved upstream commit.

## Common commands

`azldev comp make-lockless` adds selected exact names to the top-level
`lockless-components.txt` if needed, then runs the refresh pipeline.
The list is written in lexical order, one name per line without blank lines or duplicates.
Existing names and lock files are retained. Already-listed components
are still refreshed; a refresh failure leaves the list updated.

Before preparing any lockless component, rendering requires a clean project Git
repository: staged changes, unstaged tracked changes, and untracked files anywhere
in the repository block the whole invocation. Git-ignored files are excluded.
Use `--allow-uncommitted` for intentional dirty renders; `--check-only` and
`--no-git-commit` do not bypass this check. The override does not change
committed-history carryover or failure recovery.

For upstream components, rendering prepares the changelog before Release,
then writes macros, applies overlays, and updates `sources`.
Version detection and carryover use the upstream spec before overlays.
Overlays can override the prepared release and changelog.
Non-autorelease rendering then runs host `rpmdev-bumpspec`.
A temporary process-local RPM wrapper sets `_sourcedir` and `_specdir` to the spec directory
without changing `HOME` or editing the user's `.rpmmacros`; it is removed after the invocation,
including on failure.
Release edits preserve the existing spaces and tabs after `Release:`.
Rendering compares output before the final release bump; `--check-only` stops before that bump.
Unchanged lockless renders require `--no-change-rebuild`; otherwise rendering errors
without replacing existing output. For unchanged autorelease components (upstream or local),
the flag records host `date -Is` output in `.no-change-rebuild`.
Upstream non-autorelease rebuilds proceed without a timestamp marker.
Unchanged local non-autorelease components must manually update their release and changelog,
even with `--no-change-rebuild`. Comparison
ignores this root marker in both existing output and the working upstream checkout.
Lockless failures never write `RENDER_FAILED`. Before replacement, output is
untouched; failures after replacement starts clear the component directory and
use Git to restore committed output, or leave no directory if none existed.
Recovery discards uncommitted changes in that directory and keeps no backups.
Before removing existing lockless output, host `rpmspec` compares source-package NEVRs.
The package name must match. The new NEVR must be equal or higher for a final autorelease spec;
non-autorelease requires a higher NEVR. Invalid values fail with both NEVRs shown.
Validation errors leave existing output untouched and fail even without `--fail-on-error`.
First renders, `--check-only`, and dry runs skip this replacement-time check.
`--no-change-rebuild` never bypasses the NEVR check.
It replaces and automatically commits the component output directory.
The first commit also includes all staged changes, unstaged tracked changes,
and non-ignored untracked files outside the rendered output directory.
Other rendered paths are excluded even if staged; later commits include only
their component's dist-git changes.
`--changelog-comment` supplies the exact `rpmdev-bumpspec -c` value and commit
message, with no default. If omitted, `$EDITOR` or a local editor collects the
entry using a template with two blank lines and `#`-commented instructions
when no upstream changes exist. Otherwise, line 1 is blank for the summary;
non-autorelease changes start on line 2, while autorelease puts `...` on line 2
and starts changes on line 3. Each change line is prefixed with `- ` and is editable.
Blank lines and lines starting with `#` are removed, with no trailing newline;
the cleaned text is reused for the Git message. Explicit flag values remain unchanged.
Autorelease skips `rpmdev-bumpspec`; missing messages are collected before output replacement.
Autorelease with `--no-git-commit` never prompts. Blank/comment-only edited messages fail rendering.
The final Git commit never prompts; its first message line is the summary, and remaining lines are body.
Provide `--changelog-comment` for unattended rendering.
Required message prompts require both stdin and stdout to be TTYs; otherwise rendering fails.
Non-interactive renders must use `--changelog-comment` and/or `--no-git-commit`.
Upstream non-autorelease still needs `--changelog-comment` even with `--no-git-commit`.
`--no-git-commit` skips automatic staging and committing, but still renders and
bumps non-autorelease specs.
Edited upstream changes are not appended again; explicit flag messages retain the upstream Git body.
Commit refreshed TOML before rendering; configure Git author identity and install
`rpmdevtools`, `rpm-build`, and `rpmautospec` as needed.
Lockless rendering never uses mock or `rpmautospec process-distgit`; RPM macros
remain unexpanded. Lockless rendering retains all prepared dist-git files except `.git`,
without file filtering or `spectool` queries. Synthetic history
and its legacy release adjustment are skipped during rendering.

Local lockless components skip upstream carryover; Release and changelog remain unchanged.
They exclude the TOML defining the local spec path, while retaining other TOML sidecars.
They participate in unchanged-render checks and automatic commits.
For local components, `--changelog-comment` supplies only the Git message; otherwise
rendering collects it before output replacement, with commit-only instructions for non-autorelease.
Local components with `--no-git-commit` never prompt.
`--check-only` never creates project commits.

