{{ end }}
Everyday tasks (add `-q -O json` when scripting):

| Task | Command |
| --- | --- |
| List components | `azldev comp list -a` |
| Inspect one component | `azldev comp list -p <name>` |
| Add a component | `azldev comp add` |
| Build a component | `azldev comp build -p <name>` |
| Render specs | `azldev comp render -p <name>` (or `-a`) |
| Extract committed dist-git history | `azldev comp dist-git-repo <name> -o <directory>` |
| Refresh an upstream commit | `azldev comp refresh-upstream-commit -p <name>` |
| List / build images | `azldev image list` / `azldev image build` |

`comp` is an alias for `component`. Always confirm current syntax with
`azldev <command> --help`.

`comp dist-git-repo` requires exactly one component name, `--output-dir` (`-o`),
and git-filter-repo. It clones the local project's current branch with
`--single-branch --no-local`, then filters
`{{ .RenderedSpecsDir }}/<lowercase-first-letter>/<name>` into the repository root.
Only committed rendered files/history are exported; it does not fetch upstream.
Existing output requires `--force`, which deletes it after preflight checks.

For lockless components, `comp query` extracts committed rendered history into
temporary dist-git repositories and processes it with rpmautospec in Mock before
querying. Uncommitted rendered edits are ignored; locked queries still read the
working tree. Lockless `comp prepare-sources` writes directly to `--output-dir`
using render-style preparation. Current TOML and file inputs use the working tree,
including modified and untracked files. Release/changelog baselines use only
committed component dist-git files; edits in the existing dist-git directory are
ignored. Nonempty output requires `--force`; failures can
leave partial output. It downloads/generates sources before macro-file setup and
overlays, matching locked preparation. Archive overlays run before spec and
loose-file overlays. It does not compare
rendered output, apply a final render release bump, or commit. It reads render history from
`project.rendered-specs-dir` using `<lowercase-first-letter>/<component>`, never
from `--output-dir`. It never generates synthetic history. `--without-git`
removes `.git` after successful preparation, preserving it on failure.
It supports `--skip-overlays`, `--skip-sources`, and `--allow-no-hashes`.
Skipping overlays also skips macro-file setup and `sources` metadata updates;
skipping sources also skips archive overlays. Missing hashes cannot be computed
when source acquisition is skipped.
Use `comp dist-git-repo` for committed history extraction.
`comp history` continues to skip lockless components.

The hidden `advanced` group (`adv`) contains specialist integrations such as MCP and
